abstract: >-
  Bash program that runs a command and, when the command succeeds, puts what it printed on the
  clipboard, without the final newline and without colour codes, while the output still appears as
  usual. A failing command copies nothing and its exit status passes through. It reaches the
  clipboard through wl-copy, CopyQ, xclip, xsel or pbcopy, and from an SSH session through the
  terminal itself with the OSC 52 sequence. It also copies the command line with its output as a
  Markdown block, files and pictures for pasting as attachments, and secrets that are cleared after
  a delay and kept out of the clipboard history.
